    "id": "prop:certified-computation",
    "kind": "proposition",
    "statement": "For either two-score mode and every feasible branch, \\(\\mathsf A_{\\mathrm{arr}}\\) returns the same endpoint as the primal LP and the unrestricted cone dual after \\(O(|\\mathcal M_a|^2)\\) candidate intersections and \\(O(|\\mathcal M_a|^3)\\) naive arithmetic per endpoint. A separate LP computes \\(\\tau_{a,b}^r(P)\\); primal infeasibility or a dual recession ray certifies an empty branch. The statement includes parallel kink lines, zero scores, tied optima, and structural-zero cells removed before forming \\(\\mathcal J\\).",
    "free_symbols": [
      "r",
      "F_a_b_r",
      "A_arr",
      "M_a",
      "a",
      "tau_a_b_r",
      "b",
